# Normalise line endings so a Windows clone receives LF, not CRLF.
#
# Git for Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites text files on
# checkout. Most of this tree tolerates CRLF - Python, YAML, the Dockerfile and
# .env all parse either way - but GNU Make 3.81, still bundled with some Windows
# toolchains, fails on a CRLF Makefile with "missing separator". Make 4.3 and
# later handle it, so this only bites a subset of Windows setups.
#
# Forcing LF removes the class of problem rather than that one instance, and
# costs nothing: the repository is already LF throughout.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Never normalise these, whatever the detection heuristic decides.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.ico  binary
*.zip  binary
